  <section style="margin-top:52px">
    <h2 style="font-family:'Cinzel',Georgia,serif;font-size:clamp(22px,2.4vw,28px);font-weight:700;margin:0;color:#F6F1FA">Three kinds of night</h2>
    <div style="width:44px;height:2px;margin:8px 0 18px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#6FB2E8,transparent)"></div>
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(280px,1fr));gap:16px">
      <div style="position:relative;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;background:#18151F;border:1px solid #2D2838;border-radius:12px;padding:22px 20px 18px;overflow:hidden">
        <div style="position:absolute;left:0;right:0;top:0;height:3px;background:#5CCB86"></div>
        <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap">
          <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:21px;color:#F6F1FA">Nexus Night</h3>
          <span style="font-family:'Barlow Semi Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:600;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:1px 9px;border-radius:999px;border:1px solid #5CCB86;color:#5CCB86;white-space:nowrap">Casual · Weekly</span>
        </div>
        <p style="margin:0;color:#A69DB4;font-size:15px">Riot's weekly store program, the Riftbound equivalent of Friday night locals. Relaxed pairings, a Nexus Night promo pack for playing (while supplies last), and a format the store picks each week. This is the one we run every Friday.</p>
        <dl style="margin:auto 0 0;padding-top:12px;border-top:1px solid #2D2838;display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:4px 14px;font-size:14px">
          <dt style="color:#756D84;font-family:'Barlow Semi Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:12px;padding-top:2px">Format</dt><dd style="margin:0;color:#E9E4EE">Constructed, Sealed, or Modified Champion Deck</dd>
          <dt style="color:#756D84;font-family:'Barlow Semi Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:12px;padding-top:2px">Bring</dt><dd style="margin:0;color:#E9E4EE">A deck, or borrow one of ours</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div style="position:relative;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;background:#18151F;border:1px solid #2D2838;border-radius:12px;padding:22px 20px 18px;overflow:hidden">
        <div style="position:absolute;left:0;right:0;top:0;height:3px;background:#E4B45A"></div>
        <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap">
          <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:21px;color:#F6F1FA">Pre‑Rift</h3>
          <span style="font-family:'Barlow Semi Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:600;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:1px 9px;border-radius:999px;border:1px solid #E4B45A;color:#E4B45A;white-space:nowrap">Casual · Per set</span>
        </div>
        <p style="margin:0;color:#A69DB4;font-size:15px">The prerelease. About a week before each set launches, you get a Pre‑Rift kit: a 15‑card seeded Legend pack (one of six Champions), five booster packs, and a stamped Pre‑Rift promo. Build a deck from only what you opened, then play. Everything you open is yours.</p>
        <dl style="margin:auto 0 0;padding-top:12px;border-top:1px solid #2D2838;display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:4px 14px;font-size:14px">
          <dt style="color:#756D84;font-family:'Barlow Semi Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:12px;padding-top:2px">Format</dt><dd style="margin:0;color:#E9E4EE">Sealed, three best‑of‑one rounds</dd>
          <dt style="color:#756D84;font-family:'Barlow Semi Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:12px;padding-top:2px">Rules</dt><dd style="margin:0;color:#E9E4EE">Up to three domains; runes provided by the store</dd>
          <dt style="color:#756D84;font-family:'Barlow Semi Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:12px;padding-top:2px">Prizes</dt><dd style="margin:0;color:#E9E4EE">Booster packs from the new set</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div style="position:relative;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;background:#18151F;border:1px solid #2D2838;border-radius:12px;padding:22px 20px 18px;overflow:hidden">
        <div style="position:absolute;left:0;right:0;top:0;height:3px;background:#E06A58"></div>
        <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap">
          <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:21px;color:#F6F1FA">Summoner Skirmish</h3>
          <span style="font-family:'Barlow Semi Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:600;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.04em;padding:1px 9px;border-radius:999px;border:1px solid #E06A58;color:#E06A58;white-space:nowrap">Competitive · Retiring</span>
        </div>
        <p style="margin:0;color:#A69DB4;font-size:15px">The top of local competitive play in 2026. Radiance has two windows: Nov 9 – Dec 13 and Dec 14 – Jan 17, one event each. Deck registration required; tournament rules apply. No cash prizes are allowed under Riot's play policy, so store credit and boosters top up the pool. Riot is retiring the Skirmish after Radiance; these final ones run without a Regional bye. <a href="#changes">What replaces it →</a></p>
        <dl style="margin:auto 0 0;padding-top:12px;border-top:1px solid #2D2838;display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr;gap:4px 14px;font-size:14px">
          <dt style="color:#756D84;font-family:'Barlow Semi Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:12px;padding-top:2px">Format</dt><dd style="margin:0;color:#E9E4EE">1v1 Constructed, best of three</dd>
          <dt style="color:#756D84;font-family:'Barlow Semi Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:12px;padding-top:2px">Structure</dt><dd style="margin:0;color:#E9E4EE">Swiss rounds, top cut at 9+ players</dd>
          <dt style="color:#756D84;font-family:'Barlow Semi Condensed',sans-serif;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.06em;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:12px;padding-top:2px">Prizes</dt><dd style="margin:0;color:#E9E4EE">32 participation promos, 8 Top Cut promos, Champion promo and playmat</dd>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="changes" style="margin-top:52px">
    <h2 style="font-family:'Cinzel',Georgia,serif;font-size:clamp(22px,2.4vw,28px);font-weight:700;margin:0;color:#F6F1FA">What changes in 2027</h2>
    <div style="width:44px;height:2px;margin:8px 0 18px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#9B6BE0,transparent)"></div>
    <p style="color:#A69DB4;max-width:76ch;margin:0 0 18px;text-wrap:pretty">Riot's August 2026 State of Play redrew organized play. Too many Skirmish byes went unused, so the Skirmish is being split into two programs that each do one job. Pre‑Rift and Nexus Night stay exactly as they are.</p>
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(260px,1fr));gap:16px">
      <div style="background:#18151F;border:1px solid #2D2838;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px">
        <div style="font-family:'Barlow Semi Condensed',sans-serif;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:600;color:#D4A64A">New · Per set · In store</div>
        <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:20px;color:#F6F1FA">Nexus Cup</h3>
        <p style="margin:0;color:#A69DB4;font-size:15px">A store championship each set that crowns a local champion without feeding into the competitive ladder. Winner and Top 8 promos, a participation promo and a winner playmat.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#18151F;border:1px solid #2D2838;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px">
        <div style="font-family:'Barlow Semi Condensed',sans-serif;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:600;color:#E06A58">New · Curated stores</div>
        <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:20px;color:#F6F1FA">Riftbound Challenge Series</h3>
        <p style="margin:0;color:#A69DB4;font-size:15px">The first rung of the 2027 ladder and the true Skirmish successor. Instead of thousands of overlapping events, it runs through a curated network of stores each season.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#18151F;border:1px solid #2D2838;border-radius:12px;padding:20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px">
        <div style="font-family:'Barlow Semi Condensed',sans-serif;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:600;color:#6FB2E8">Platform</div>
        <h3 style="margin:0;font-size:20px;color:#F6F1FA">PlayRiftbound.com</h3>
        <p style="margin:0;color:#A69DB4;font-size:15px">Store events are moving off Carde.io to Riot's own platform, starting with Radiance events. Make an account there before your next event.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top:14px;font-size:14px;color:#756D84">Above the store: Regional Qualifiers become Riftbound Regionals (3–4 per set), Regional Championships become Continentals (four per year, three days each), and a World Championship caps the season. Unused Skirmish byes stay valid at Regionals through 2027. Source: <a href="https://playriftbound.com/en-us/news/organizedplay/august-2026-state-of-play">August 2026 State of Play</a>.</div>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top:52px;position:relative;padding:30px 34px;border:1px solid #6B5628;border-radius:16px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(32,28,41,.92),rgba(20,17,27,.92));box-shadow:0 30px 60px -30px rgba(0,0,0,.9),inset 0 1px 0 rgba(230,189,102,.12)">
