  <section style="margin-top:52px">
    <h2 style="font-family:'Cinzel',Georgia,serif;font-size:clamp(22px,2.4vw,28px);font-weight:700;margin:0;color:#F6F1FA">Playing and collecting</h2>
    <div style="width:44px;height:2px;margin:8px 0 18px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,#6FB2E8,transparent)"></div>
    <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(260px,1fr));gap:16px">
      <div style="background:#18151F;border:1px solid #2D2838;border-radius:12px;padding:20px">
        <h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-size:20px;color:#F6F1FA">At the table</h3>
        <p style="margin:0;color:#A69DB4;font-size:15px">Nexus Night is casual by design: learn‑to‑play games, deck tuning, and the occasional bracket when enough Legends show up. Bring a deck or borrow one.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#18151F;border:1px solid #2D2838;border-radius:12px;padding:20px">
        <h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-size:20px;color:#F6F1FA">Singles, sealed, graded</h3>
        <p style="margin:0;color:#A69DB4;font-size:15px">The collection spans loose singles, sealed product, and a handful of graded cards. All of it lives in Collectr under the showcase handle <span style="font-family:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;color:#6FB2E8">@undrwrldcub</span>.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#18151F;border:1px solid #2D2838;border-radius:12px;padding:20px">
        <h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-size:20px;color:#F6F1FA">Value over time</h3>
        <p style="margin:0;color:#A69DB4;font-size:15px">A tracker workbook takes regular snapshots: total portfolio value, per‑card price trends, and which cards are climbing or sliding between snapshots.</p>
      </div>
      <div style="background:#18151F;border:1px solid #2D2838;border-radius:12px;padding:20px">
        <h3 style="margin:0 0 6px;font-size:20px;color:#F6F1FA">Real spend, real ROI</h3>
        <p style="margin:0;color:#A69DB4;font-size:15px">Market value is one number. Cash actually spent is another. The tracker keeps both, so the honest return on the hobby is always one column away.</p>
      </div>
